<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8"?>
<task id="020" project="spaarke-auth-v4-dataverse-MI">
  <metadata>
    <title>Build the IClientAssertionProvider seam and raise the ADR-010 ceiling (FR-B1)</title>
    <phase>2 Provider</phase>
    <gate>011 complete</gate>
    <status>not-started</status>
    <rigor>FULL</rigor>
    <rigor-reason>auth tag, NEW component, cross-assembly architecture, touches a live CI gate.</rigor-reason>
    <model-tier>opus</model-tier>
    <model-tier-reason>Architectural seam spanning two assemblies under a CI-enforced layer constraint; a wrong shape here propagates to every downstream task.</model-tier-reason>
    <effort>xhigh</effort>
    <parallel-group>B</parallel-group>
    <parallel-safe>false</parallel-safe>
    <parallel-reason>Everything in Phase 2 onward depends on this seam; must land alone.</parallel-reason>
    <deps>011</deps>
    <tags>auth,bff-api,dataverse,architecture,new-component</tags>
    <estimated-effort>1 day</estimated-effort>
  </metadata>

  <prompt>Introduce a one-method IClientAssertionProvider contract declared in Spaarke.Dataverse, with ManagedIdentityAssertionProvider implemented in the BFF, so all confidential clients can obtain a MI-issued client assertion. Raise the ADR010_DITests 1:1-interface ceiling in the same PR — it will otherwise fail the build.</prompt>
  <role>SPAARKE platform architect. Respect the CI-enforced shared-library layering absolutely.</role>
  <goal>A registered singleton assertion provider, injected as a nullable parameter into the shared-lib types, with all 46 existing test fixtures still compiling and green.</goal>

  <justification>
    <existing>No assertion abstraction exists anywhere — verified: zero WithClientAssertion / ClientAssertionCredential in src/**. ManagedIdentityCredentialFactory.cs:26-41 provides a UAMI-pinned TokenCredential for Azure.Identity app-only calls, but no MSAL client assertion and no CCA cache; it is used by none of the 8 CCA sites.</existing>
    <extension>The IMPLEMENTATION extends the existing Infrastructure/Auth/ seam and reuses ManagedIdentityCredentialFactory's UAMI resolution. The CONTRACT cannot live there: Spaarke.Dataverse cannot reference Sprk.Bff.Api (dependency direction) and cannot reference Spaarke.Core (circular — Spaarke.Core.csproj:32 already references Dataverse; blocked by LayerDependencyTests.cs:43 FR-14). Dependency inversion is the only legal seam.</extension>
    <cost-of-doing-nothing>Without it, DataverseAccessDataSource and the other shared-lib sites cannot obtain a client assertion at all, so the OBO paths — including row-level authorization for every document and AI endpoint — must keep using the client secret. The project's primary goal fails. Additionally each of the 6 call sites would need independent assertion plumbing, and the credential type could not be switched by configuration, which is the entire rollback mechanism (NFR-06).</cost-of-doing-nothing>
  </justification>

  <context>
    <background>E4' established that Microsoft.Identity.Web's declarative ClientCredentials list is unusable here — zero EnableTokenAcquisition / ITokenAcquisition / IDownstreamApi / ClientCredentials in any .cs, and Spaarke.Dataverse has no Identity.Web reference at all. The mechanism is .WithClientAssertion + ManagedIdentityClientAssertion. The seam shape mirrors the nullable TokenCredential already injected at DataverseAccessDataSource.cs:32 from Program.cs:46-48.</background>
    <relevant-files>
      <file role="new">src/server/shared/Spaarke.Dataverse/IClientAssertionProvider.cs</file>
      <file role="new">src/server/api/Sprk.Bff.Api/Infrastructure/Auth/ManagedIdentityAssertionProvider.cs</file>
      <file role="canonical-reference">src/server/api/Sprk.Bff.Api/Infrastructure/Auth/ManagedIdentityCredentialFactory.cs</file>
      <file role="canonical-reference">src/server/shared/Spaarke.Dataverse/DataverseAccessDataSource.cs</file>
      <file role="modify">tests/Spaarke.ArchTests/ADR010_DITests.cs</file>
      <file role="modify">src/server/api/Sprk.Bff.Api/Sprk.Bff.Api.csproj</file>
    </relevant-files>
    <dependencies><dependency task="011" status="pending">Singleton-cached CCAs — assertions require shared clients</dependency></dependencies>
  </context>

  <constraints>
    <constraint source="project">Scope: the CONTRACT is declared in Spaarke.Dataverse; the IMPLEMENTATION and Microsoft.Identity.Web.Certificateless live in the BFF ONLY. Spaarke.Dataverse gains NO ProjectReference and NO new PackageReference.</constraint>
    <constraint source="ADR-010">Scope: raise knownOneToOneCeiling in ADR010_DITests.cs:164 from 153 to 154 IN THIS PR, with a comment citing this project and the FR-14 cross-assembly justification — the maintenance procedure the test's own comment documents at :144-146. Without it the build fails.</constraint>
    <constraint source="ADR-010">Scope: register the provider inside an existing DI feature module. Do NOT add an inline AddSingleton to Program.cs — ADR-010 MUST NOT "inline registrations". The TokenCredential precedent at Program.cs:46-48 is itself inline and must not be mirrored.</constraint>
    <constraint source="ADR-028">Scope: use ManagedIdentityClientAssertion and REUSE the instance — it caches the signed assertion until expiry.</constraint>
    <constraint source="project">Scope: shared-lib constructors take IClientAssertionProvider? assertion = null with a NULL DEFAULT. Adding a required parameter breaks all 46 test fixtures (NFR-04).</constraint>
    <constraint source="project">Scope: do NOT migrate any call site in this task — that is task 022. This task only creates and registers the seam.</constraint>
  </constraints>

  <knowledge>
    <topic>Client assertions, dependency inversion, shared-library layering</topic>
    <files>
      <file>.claude/adr/ADR-028-spaarke-auth-architecture.md</file>
      <file>.claude/adr/ADR-010-di-minimalism.md</file>
      <file>.claude/constraints/auth.md</file>
      <file>.claude/constraints/bff-extensions.md</file>
      <file>src/server/shared/CLAUDE.md</file>
      <file>projects/spaarke-auth-v4-dataverse-MI/notes/PHASE-0-LIVE-VERIFICATION.md</file>
    </files>
  </knowledge>

  <steps mode="prescriptive">
    <step>Declare IClientAssertionProvider (one method returning Task&lt;string&gt;, taking a CancellationToken) in Spaarke.Dataverse.</step>
    <step>Add Microsoft.Identity.Web.Certificateless to Sprk.Bff.Api.csproj ONLY.</step>
    <step>Implement ManagedIdentityAssertionProvider in Infrastructure/Auth/, reusing ManagedIdentityCredentialFactory's UAMI resolution; cache the ManagedIdentityClientAssertion instance.</step>
    <step>Register it as a singleton in an existing DI feature module (not Program.cs).</step>
    <step>Add the nullable parameter to the shared-lib constructors WITHOUT changing behaviour yet.</step>
    <step>Raise ADR010_DITests.cs:164 ceiling 153 to 154 with the justification comment.</step>
    <step>Run dotnet test tests/Spaarke.ArchTests/ and confirm both FR-14 and the ADR-010 ceiling pass.</step>
    <step>Measure publish size (Certificateless is new) and run the CVE scan.</step>
  </steps>

  <escalation>
    <trigger>Adding Certificateless pulls a transitive package that raises publish size by 5 MB or more, or introduces a HIGH CVE — STOP and report per CLAUDE.md §10.</trigger>
    <trigger>The nullable parameter still breaks test fixtures — STOP; NFR-04 is a hard constraint and the seam shape is wrong if it does.</trigger>
  </escalation>

  <outputs>
    <output type="new">src/server/shared/Spaarke.Dataverse/IClientAssertionProvider.cs</output>
    <output type="new">src/server/api/Sprk.Bff.Api/Infrastructure/Auth/ManagedIdentityAssertionProvider.cs</output>
    <output type="modify">tests/Spaarke.ArchTests/ADR010_DITests.cs</output>
    <output type="modify">src/server/api/Sprk.Bff.Api/Sprk.Bff.Api.csproj</output>
  </outputs>

  <acceptance-criteria>
    <criterion>Spaarke.Dataverse.csproj shows NO added ProjectReference and NO added PackageReference.</criterion>
    <criterion>LayerDependencyTests FR-14 passes unmodified.</criterion>
    <criterion>ADR010_DITests passes with the ceiling at 154 and a justification comment naming this project.</criterion>
    <criterion>The provider is registered in a feature module; Program.cs gains no new inline AddSingleton.</criterion>
    <criterion>All 46 existing test fixtures compile and pass unchanged.</criterion>
    <criterion>Negative case: resolving the provider twice returns the same singleton and the same cached assertion instance.</criterion>
    <criterion>Negative case: with no managed identity present (local dev), the provider fails gracefully rather than throwing at startup.</criterion>
    <criterion>Publish size + delta reported vs 44.96 MB; no new HIGH CVE; Placement Justification stated in the PR.</criterion>
  </acceptance-criteria>
</task>
